    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8e7caae8_ae593010",
        "filename": "common/mkbp_event.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 99,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-07-16T20:45:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When we make external calls (i.e. host_set_single_event in this case) when interrupts are disabled, we cannot guarantee that the implementation does not call into task scheduling (and deschedules itself in a some code path).\n\nIf we deschedule our task while interrupts are off, then we are in a scheduling deadlock.\n\nThis happened with ISH and mkbp_set_host_active_via_heci\n\nBasically my new rule for disabling interrupts is to ensure that the enabling/disabling code reasonably controls all code paths in a way that won\u0027t call into task scheduling.",
      "parentUuid": "fee6e5da_e2b7bacd",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 98,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 99,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "45811fcfa1128948ff7930df65258c1405a9bdfa",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c15d4474_ca716950",
        "filename": "include/config.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 2686,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003000
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-07-15T23:37:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Just a final thought: If you name this CONFIG_MKBP_WAKE_USE_HOST_EVENT, then you don\u0027t need to add check for both CONFIG_MKBP_USE_GPIO and CONFIG_MKBP_USE_GPIO_AND_HOST_EVENT in all the places. For x86 boards you can also auto define CONFIG_MKBP_WAKE_USE_HOST_EVENT if CONFIG_MKBP_USE_GPIO is set since we know that for x86 it is required to set the host event to cause a wake.\n\nJust trying to avoid having too many options for MKBP_USE since it can get confusing when adding new boards. I will leave it upto you to make the final call.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2686,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 2686,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "45811fcfa1128948ff7930df65258c1405a9bdfa",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
